  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 河\ntitle: river; watercourse\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 水\nradicalNumber: 85\nonyomi: [カ]\nkunyomi: [かわ]\ndistractors: [何, 向, 池]\n---\n\n# 河 — river; watercourse\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 水 (no. 85) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n河 concerns a river. 河 かわ and 川 かわ are spellings of the same native river word. 河川 かせん supplies the on reading カ; it means rivers or river systems.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Notice 氵 beside 可 and imagine a river passing a small opening. This is a modern-shape memory aid, not a claim about the character's historical construction or phonetic role.\n\nThe canonical radical 水, no. 85, appears as the three left-hand dots 氵.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| カ | on | 河川 かせん - rivers |\n| かわ | kun | [河](../words/河.md) かわ - river; stream |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [河](../words/河.md) かわ - river; stream\n- 河川 かせん - rivers\n- 氷河 ひょうが - glacier\n- [運河](../words/運河.md) うんが - canal\n\n## Notes\n\n- [川](川.md) and 河 overlap in river meaning. The linked word article recommends 川 for ordinary beginner writing; large river equals 河 is not a universal spelling rule.\n- 氷河 ひょうが demonstrates a voiced ガ inside that compound. Learn its complete reading; this does not replace the independent native reading かわ.\n- Distinguish [何](何.md), what, with 亻 on the left. Similar-looking components do not make 何 another river character.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1172710, 1193520, 1390020, 1488880.\n",
